    "title": "Corrupted wallet when upgrading to 31.1",
    "body": "### Is there an existing issue for this?\n\n- [x] I have searched the existing issues\n\n### Current behaviour\n\nI updated to 31.1 from 29.2 and it resulted in a wallet.dat getting corrupted, here is my log:\n```\n2026-08-12T19:37:55Z init message: Loading wallet…\n2026-08-12T19:37:55Z [FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3] Last client version = 290200\n2026-08-12T19:37:55Z [FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3] The descriptor ID calculated by the wallet differs from the one in DB\n2026-08-12T19:37:56Z [FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3] Setting spkMan to active: id = 1b38ccf1fb798d491b870edbf10b9801eae05c458a95c26bfb585a96b9cd04e7, type = bech32m, internal = false\n2026-08-12T19:37:56Z [FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3] Setting spkMan to active: id = 9fefd4023c79247585ff8c766b5654319e0fef7d03c1b79fb10fc8f045b1a449, type = bech32m, internal = true\n2026-08-12T19:37:56Z [FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3] Releasing wallet FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3..\n2026-08-12T19:37:56Z [error] Error loading /Home/Library/Application Support/Bitcoin/FullyNoded-36d0229102d0812082856404228e8b2a8f7a6eb5856c5e9e6333bb079e9481a3/wallet.dat: Wallet corrupted\n```\n\nHow is `The descriptor ID` calculated? All I did was shut the node down, delete old binaries and install new binaries.\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nUpgrade without wallet corruption.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI can not remember the details of the wallet off the top of my head, can hopefully find my backup. \n\n### Relevant log output\n\n_No response_\n\n### How did you obtain Bitcoin Core\n\nPre-built binaries\n\n### What version of Bitcoin Core are you using?\n\nv31.1\n\n### Operating system and version\n\nMacos 15.3\n\n### Machine specifications\n\n_No response_",
